WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.460
Gotansha Publishing

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:07.630
Oh my God...

00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:10.040
He passed away...?

00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:15.330
Obituary:
Yasuyuki Mimura
He died of heart failure on the 10th
of this month at the age of 45.
He was the Managing Director of Konitika LTD.

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:15.330
It may be inconsiderate to admit
that this is one way we writers find new material.

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:17.630
So checking the obituaries
is part of my daily routine.

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:23.040
I always keep funeral attire in my locker...

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:26.250
These are for summer.

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:28.170
That's right...

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:30.760
Some of my winter clothes got burned
while I was smoking

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:33.080
and I forgot I was supposed to buy new ones.

00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:39.010
I'm going to freeze in this...

00:00:57.630 --> 00:01:02.010
Shigoto dekiru otoko sore ga kanojo no konomi

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:06.300
Kiai irete tsutometa no daga

00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:08.870
Isogashii wa tsuman nai wa

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:13.540
Ima no kaisha kanari level takai hou dashi

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:17.710
Oyaji garami no kone mo aru kara

00:01:17.830 --> 00:01:19.870
Yameru wakya nai shi

00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:38.290
Itsumo boku wa hitori kiri

00:01:38.290 --> 00:01:43.460
Furo ni haitte neru dake

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:48.880
Nagameru koto sae dekinai

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:55.340
Kimi no kami o aruku sugata o

00:01:55.500 --> 00:02:00.630
Nerukoto shika dekinai

00:02:01.210 --> 00:02:06.880
Semete yume no naka de demo

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:08.880
Kimi ni aitai

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:16.410
Accomplished Hataraki Man

00:02:12.250 --> 00:02:14.290
"Accomplished Hataraki Man."

00:02:16.420 --> 00:02:19.000
Funeral
for
Yasuyuki Mimura

00:02:19.330 --> 00:02:21.960
He was just 45 years old...

00:02:22.330 --> 00:02:25.620
He collapsed 7 days ago after suffering
a brain hemorrhage, and then...

00:02:26.130 --> 00:02:27.670
Taken from us too soon...

00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:31.410
He always said working until
the middle of the night was the norm...

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:34.000
Another death from overwork...

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:40.920
I was scheduled to interview this man
for an article next week.

00:02:42.210 --> 00:02:44.380
Are you sure you want to be in charge
of that special issue?

00:02:44.630 --> 00:02:47.300
Yeah! It effectively makes me the editor-in-chief!

00:02:47.290 --> 00:02:51.040
The editor-in-chief... meaning you have
to do everything by yourself.

00:02:51.710 --> 00:02:54.250
You still have to take care
of your normal workload on top of it, right?

00:02:54.460 --> 00:02:56.630
Of course. It's a supplemental issue.

00:02:56.960 --> 00:03:00.790
That's just going to build emotional stress,
leaving you physically and mentally exhausted.

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:03.830
Want me to make your funeral arrangements?

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:06.000
Doctors shouldn't joke about death!

00:03:08.170 --> 00:03:11.380
Starting tomorrow, I'm going out for interviews
and will have 3 weeks to finish the entire issue.

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:15.080
Last week I submitted a pitch for an extended
version of my "Seven Samurai" article,

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:17.750
and it became the main feature of next month's
supplemental issue of Weekly JIDAI.

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:20.210
Doesn't "The Fifty Samurai" just sound cool?

00:03:20.540 --> 00:03:22.750
Hey... what are you doing?

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:24.170
Breast cancer check.

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:29.410
You realize if you just keep investing yourself
in work, you'll never make progress with your man!

00:03:30.330 --> 00:03:32.460
So that's why you're in a bad mood today...

00:03:33.330 --> 00:03:35.910
It's okay, I'll make progress on both sides.

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:37.340
Love and work!

00:03:37.330 --> 00:03:39.790
Don't pretend your life is like
some picture-perfect commercial on TV!

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:42.870
You're most likely to get sick
when put under stress like that!

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:45.080
I'm not reckless enough to get sick!

00:03:45.330 --> 00:03:48.540
After all, this is my first chance
to prove myself with a major editorial project.

00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:52.880
I really want to meet with them all in person, but...

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:56.130
The "Seven Samurai" interviews
will be reprinted, which means...

00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:58.000
I have 43 spots left to fill.

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:02.630
There's 5 writers working on this,
so each one of them should cover 7 or 8 people...

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:04.790
leaving just 3 for me.

00:04:06.170 --> 00:04:08.880
But this is a rare opportunity, so I'd like to do more.

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:12.540
Then I'll make myself responsible
for 8 of them instead...

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:13.620
Matsukata!

00:04:13.630 --> 00:04:14.340
Yes?

00:04:14.710 --> 00:04:17.710
Narita-san wanted to make sure you know not
to be late on proofreading that earthquake article.

00:04:17.710 --> 00:04:19.630
Oh... okay.

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:22.210
I forgot, I still have other work to do.

00:04:22.790 --> 00:04:25.080
Which means I'll only have time
for 5 of these at most.

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:28.410
This one... this one... and...

00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:30.130
Yasuyuki Mimura...

00:04:31.210 --> 00:04:35.540
His company "Konitika LTD" started out
as no more than a simple internet venture,

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:38.800
but thanks to his efforts,
it became an industry-leading web portal.

00:04:39.130 --> 00:04:43.840
He is also responsible for establishing a free
computer school for children, among other things.

00:04:43.830 --> 00:04:47.410
He's made many notable contributions to society
that will continue to be recognized... wow.

00:04:48.290 --> 00:04:51.830
If we want Japan to be able
to thrive on a more global scale,

00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:55.620
then we as a country should focus
on cooperation instead of competition.

00:04:57.380 --> 00:05:01.760
To be honest... I wanted to meet him in person
to find out if those are his real thoughts.

00:05:02.750 --> 00:05:06.750
Ah, hello? I'm sorry for the sudden call.

00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:10.040
I'm Matsukata from the editorial department
of Weekly JIDAI Magazine.

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:12.580
I'm calling in regards to setting up
an interview with Mimura-san.

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:14.210
Ah, hello. This is Mimura speaking.

00:05:14.420 --> 00:05:15.710
Um, let's see...

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:17.500
It's actually him!

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:20.340
I'm open the 16th at 2:15 PM.

00:05:20.830 --> 00:05:22.710
Would it be possible for you to come to my office?

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:23.460
Of course!

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:27.710
Mimura-san, do you always manage
your schedule without any assistance?

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:31.420
Yes. If I decide my schedule personally
then I find it easier to keep track of.

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:36.260
From what I could tell over the phone,
Mimura-san was very busy.

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:39.790
Yet, the tone of his voice was lively
and his attitude was positive.

00:05:40.130 --> 00:05:42.510
I never felt even a small trace
of fatigue coming from him.

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:44.000
And yet...

00:05:44.540 --> 00:05:50.580
Obituary:
Yasuyuki Mimura
He died of heart failure on the 10th
of this month at the age of 45.
He was the Managing Director of Konitika LTD.

00:05:45.670 --> 00:05:49.550
Before we could have our interview,
Mimura-san left this world forever.

00:05:53.250 --> 00:05:55.540
People who live by filling up
the empty space in their lives...

00:05:57.580 --> 00:06:02.040
Mimura-san... I've thought of another question
that I wanted to ask you.

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:07.420
When they've filled up all the empty space...

00:06:08.420 --> 00:06:10.000
do people die?

00:06:14.130 --> 00:06:15.760
Hello? Shinji?

00:06:16.290 --> 00:06:19.080
We're on for the day after tomorrow.
I reserved that French place we talked about.

00:06:19.670 --> 00:06:21.460
What's wrong? You seem down.

00:06:21.460 --> 00:06:23.000
Ah... yeah.

00:06:23.500 --> 00:06:27.170
Well I'm working on a special issue
called "The Fifty Samurai," but...

00:06:27.540 --> 00:06:30.460
one of the people I planned
to interview passed away suddenly.

00:06:30.920 --> 00:06:32.630
Today I went to his funeral...

00:06:33.290 --> 00:06:36.790
All I had were summer clothes,
so both my heart and body were pretty chilled.

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:39.380
Hey... Shinji?

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:40.250
Huh?

00:06:41.630 --> 00:06:43.420
I'm more lonely than usual tonight...

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:46.170
Come warm me up.

00:06:51.630 --> 00:06:52.630
Right now?

00:06:53.460 --> 00:06:56.750
No can do. I have a meeting scheduled
first thing tomorrow morning.

00:06:59.420 --> 00:07:01.590
Ah... okay, I'm sorry.

00:07:02.920 --> 00:07:05.590
Bye, then... Goodnight...

00:07:05.580 --> 00:07:06.910
Yeah, goodnight.

00:07:16.210 --> 00:07:17.500
I figured he was busy.

00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:19.580
But I wanted to be bold for once!

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:24.370
Right now?

00:07:27.670 --> 00:07:31.050
He's never... used that tone of voice before.

00:07:36.330 --> 00:07:37.710
I have to go over those documents.

00:07:39.040 --> 00:07:41.420
Half of the interviews are done at this point,

00:07:41.420 --> 00:07:43.920
and tomorrow I'll start writing the drafts
in between more interviews.

00:07:45.750 --> 00:07:48.040
For some reason, I can't get focused.

00:07:51.250 --> 00:07:54.500
Oh, that's right. We have
the usual weekly meeting tomorrow, too.

00:07:54.790 --> 00:07:57.580
There's still so much that I need to get done, but...

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:00.330
Right now?

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:05.160
Those words... stung hard enough to distract me.

00:08:14.750 --> 00:08:16.210
I have to get in bed...

00:08:21.250 --> 00:08:22.250
I'm freezing.

00:08:22.580 --> 00:08:25.330
Shit... I might have caught a cold.

00:08:31.330 --> 00:08:33.000
I shouldn't have checked...

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:35.460
I'm such an idiot!

00:08:35.960 --> 00:08:39.090
I can't afford to deal with a fever right now!

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:43.290
Oh, Matsukata, are you sick?

00:08:43.290 --> 00:08:44.870
Please don't spread it around.

00:08:45.080 --> 00:08:47.750
I'm sorry... I'll do my best
not to pass it on to anyone.

00:08:47.750 --> 00:08:49.670
Please keep your distance from me.

00:08:53.250 --> 00:08:55.380
Why don't you just take a sick day?

00:08:55.540 --> 00:08:57.000
You look like a bug in a cocoon.

00:08:57.420 --> 00:08:59.710
If I don't work, then my special issue
won't get printed...

00:08:59.710 --> 00:09:00.840
Hey, Matsukata!

00:09:00.830 --> 00:09:01.370
Yes?

00:09:01.750 --> 00:09:03.920
Apparently that writer, Kawamura-san,
is in the hospital.

00:09:03.920 --> 00:09:05.050
What?!

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:06.830
His wife is on line 6 right now.

00:09:08.460 --> 00:09:11.670
Hello? This is Matsukata speaking.

00:09:12.170 --> 00:09:13.090
Yes...

00:09:15.210 --> 00:09:16.290
Oh, really?

00:09:17.380 --> 00:09:19.590
Ah... um...

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:22.540
I hate to ask this of him right now, but...

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:26.420
Could he complete any part of his manuscript,
or at least the interviews?

00:09:26.920 --> 00:09:29.250
I'll wait until the last possible minute
before the deadline...

00:09:29.580 --> 00:09:32.620
My husband is suffering from a severe case
of pneumonia right now!

00:09:32.630 --> 00:09:34.170
Do you want him to die?!

00:09:34.750 --> 00:09:35.460
Um...

00:09:36.250 --> 00:09:39.500
I mean, Kawamura-san always works very fast...

00:09:39.790 --> 00:09:42.670
That's why I asked him to do 10 of them,
and he already interviewed 6.

00:09:43.330 --> 00:09:45.660
Damn it... I can't think straight!

00:09:46.540 --> 00:09:48.670
Um... I'm terribly sorry.

00:09:49.540 --> 00:09:50.460
Um...

00:09:58.880 --> 00:10:00.590
Matsukata, are you okay?

00:10:00.580 --> 00:10:03.790
Things are slowly starting
to spiral out of my control.

00:10:04.420 --> 00:10:07.750
Well... it may only be a supplemental issue,
but you are the editor-in-chief.

00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:11.000
That's a rare opportunity around here,
so do your best.

00:10:11.420 --> 00:10:13.000
Um... Narita-san?

00:10:13.540 --> 00:10:14.250
Huh?

00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:16.590
Do you happen to know
of any writers who are available?

00:10:17.420 --> 00:10:20.300
Kawamura-san collapsed... and is in the hospita-

00:10:20.290 --> 00:10:23.870
One of your best qualities is how you do your job
without relying on anyone else for help.

00:10:23.880 --> 00:10:25.710
But... um...

00:10:25.880 --> 00:10:28.090
You should cherish that trait
and continue to develop it.

00:10:28.960 --> 00:10:31.540
In other words... "Don't ask me"...

00:10:34.830 --> 00:10:39.000
That spat with Dojima-san caused me to fall
out of favor with a bunch of the writers around here.

00:10:39.290 --> 00:10:42.580
These five were the only ones who agreed to help,
so there are no replacements.

00:10:43.630 --> 00:10:47.380
Which means, all I can do is divide up the
remainder of Kawamura-san's work among them.

00:10:49.250 --> 00:10:51.380
Huh? With this little time left?

00:10:51.380 --> 00:10:54.340
Please! Ito-kun, you're the only one I have left!

00:10:54.710 --> 00:10:56.210
Okay? Okay!

00:10:56.210 --> 00:10:56.960
Ah, but...

00:10:56.960 --> 00:10:59.210
Matsukata! Your writer, Komatsu-san, is on line 3.

00:10:59.210 --> 00:11:00.290
Coming!

00:11:00.710 --> 00:11:02.130
Okay, I'm counting on you, Ito-kun.

00:11:04.460 --> 00:11:06.460
Hello, this is Matsukata. Thanks for your hard work.

00:11:07.420 --> 00:11:11.300
Yes, that's right... could you please
cover 2 more of them for me?

00:11:11.710 --> 00:11:14.710
Yes... yes... is there any way?

00:11:15.080 --> 00:11:17.460
Ito-kun? Yes, I've already asked him.

00:11:17.920 --> 00:11:20.340
Yes... of course I'm working on some as well.

00:11:21.080 --> 00:11:25.870
Well... this is my project to begin with,
so it's only natural that I also work on it.

00:11:26.460 --> 00:11:28.500
Including suffering all of the consequences.

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:30.160
A spiral of disasters...

00:11:30.170 --> 00:11:32.880
Hospital

00:11:33.750 --> 00:11:35.000
Ouch! Ow, ow, ow...

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:35.880
You do realize...

00:11:36.170 --> 00:11:38.590
even with this shot, you won't get better
without some proper sleep.

00:11:38.920 --> 00:11:41.050
Also, you're prohibited from consuming
any alcohol or tobacco.

00:11:41.420 --> 00:11:43.590
I'm not in the mood even if I could...

00:11:44.040 --> 00:11:46.580
You didn't even have the willpower
to get properly dressed today.

00:11:47.130 --> 00:11:48.800
No earrings, not even makeup!

00:11:49.540 --> 00:11:51.540
I'll wear anything as long as it keeps me warm...

00:11:53.380 --> 00:11:55.800
Today I'm going to interview Mimura-san's wife...

00:11:56.170 --> 00:11:58.130
And after I transcribe the tape, I'll get some sleep.

00:12:03.710 --> 00:12:05.040
I'm so sorry about this...

00:12:05.040 --> 00:12:09.580
I know he just barely passed away, but I didn't
want to remove your husband from my article.

00:12:10.920 --> 00:12:14.250
That's okay... I think he would be overjoyed.

00:12:15.580 --> 00:12:16.910
Thank you very much.

00:12:18.290 --> 00:12:19.580
Oh, you poor thing...

00:12:19.580 --> 00:12:21.410
Did you recently catch that cold?

00:12:22.000 --> 00:12:23.630
Ah... I'm sorry.

00:12:23.960 --> 00:12:27.460
I'm trying to avoid letting it spread by wearing
this mask, so forgive me if it seems rude.

00:12:27.830 --> 00:12:29.000
Just wait here.

00:12:29.000 --> 00:12:31.290
I'll go put on some ginger tea for you.

00:12:31.630 --> 00:12:33.340
It's very effective against colds.

00:12:35.460 --> 00:12:38.130
I'm sorry... you don't have to worry about me.

00:12:39.710 --> 00:12:41.880
We always treat colds around here with this.

00:12:42.630 --> 00:12:44.130
I appreciate your kindness.

00:12:51.630 --> 00:12:54.760
I knew it would be...
but this is so emotionally draining.

00:12:55.290 --> 00:12:57.670
I wonder if it's too soon for her to talk about him.

00:13:00.250 --> 00:13:02.920
Maybe I'm being too stubborn
because it's my first major project...

00:13:03.630 --> 00:13:05.460
Or maybe I'm just a cheap sentimentalist?

00:13:06.630 --> 00:13:07.960
It's delicious.

00:13:08.250 --> 00:13:09.420
And really warming me up.

00:13:09.670 --> 00:13:11.590
I see, that's a relief.

00:13:12.380 --> 00:13:17.260
I... went so far as to drag a widow into all of this,
but for what purpose exactly?

00:13:18.080 --> 00:13:22.500
My husband... would also work
through his sickness just like you are.

00:13:23.290 --> 00:13:26.120
"If I work, then I'll get better," He used to say.

00:13:26.960 --> 00:13:29.540
Even if I told him to rest,
he just simply wouldn't listen.

00:13:29.880 --> 00:13:31.130
The day he died...

00:13:31.290 --> 00:13:33.000
he hadn't slept for days.

00:13:33.630 --> 00:13:37.670
Just when I thought he was coming home to rest,
all he would talk about was his job.

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:41.040
And when he left the house,
he looked at me and said...

00:13:42.170 --> 00:13:43.210
Don't push yourself.

00:13:43.580 --> 00:13:45.160
Those were his last words to me.

00:13:45.670 --> 00:13:48.880
Isn't that strange?
For him of all people to say that...

00:13:49.380 --> 00:13:50.590
In that instant...

00:13:51.210 --> 00:13:54.670
I strongly felt the impact
Mimura-san left on this world.

00:13:56.330 --> 00:13:58.960
Just because someone's busy
doesn't mean they're doing good work.

00:13:59.710 --> 00:14:02.000
Thank you for talking with me.

00:14:02.500 --> 00:14:05.540
And also... for the tea, I really appreciate it.

00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:09.420
People aren't admirable
just because they do good work, either.

00:14:09.830 --> 00:14:12.870
What exactly is it that I want
to convey through this project?

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:15.870
I don't want to just make
a catalog of success stories...

00:14:16.380 --> 00:14:18.210
There has to be something more at the core of it all.

00:14:20.750 --> 00:14:23.790
Matsukata-san... promise us you won't freak out.

00:14:24.790 --> 00:14:26.170
What's going on?

00:14:27.170 --> 00:14:29.710
This came in the mail from Ito-kun...

00:14:30.080 --> 00:14:34.460
As his last act of good will,
he said he left you the interview tapes...

00:14:35.500 --> 00:14:40.670
Dear Matsukata-san,
I'm leaving to go
and rediscover myself.
-Ito

00:14:35.750 --> 00:14:40.210
Dear Matsukata-san, I'm leaving
to go and rediscover myself. Ito.

00:14:42.540 --> 00:14:44.170
What the hell?!

00:14:44.170 --> 00:14:46.300
Ito

00:14:46.290 --> 00:14:47.210
Gone AWOL

00:14:49.380 --> 00:14:51.380
He already transcribed 3 of the interview tapes.

00:14:51.380 --> 00:14:54.010
That means 5 more to transcribe
before I can write the articles.

00:14:54.790 --> 00:14:56.040
Wait a second!

00:14:56.040 --> 00:14:59.080
I haven't even finished mine
or Kawamura-san's part yet!

00:15:04.460 --> 00:15:05.090
Sorry.

00:15:05.080 --> 00:15:06.120
No can do.

00:15:07.460 --> 00:15:09.340
My schedule is full this week.

00:15:08.630 --> 00:15:10.460
Impossible

00:15:09.330 --> 00:15:11.410
I'm pretty busy myself...

00:15:10.460 --> 00:15:11.500
Impossible
No go

00:15:13.540 --> 00:15:14.500
Useless

00:15:15.750 --> 00:15:25.960
Maiko Kaji (31)
Editorial Staff of Weekly JIDAI

00:15:16.630 --> 00:15:20.630
As a ground rule, I never get involved
in other people's work.
Oh yeah, a sweet voice

00:15:20.630 --> 00:15:22.130
Matsukata submitted the pitch for this supplemental
issue herself, which is all the more reason not to.

00:15:22.130 --> 00:15:25.960
Matsukata submitted the pitch for this supplemental
issue herself, which is all the more reason not to.
It must be for you baby

00:15:26.210 --> 00:15:29.590
Of course... everyone is a little jealous of her, too.

00:15:29.920 --> 00:15:33.920
Memories ride the night train

00:15:39.630 --> 00:15:43.800
I stay awake until morning

00:15:44.290 --> 00:15:48.960
Hiroko Matsukata

00:15:44.290 --> 00:15:51.120
Just gazing at the light of the stars

00:15:52.460 --> 00:15:56.250
There was no particular reason

00:15:57.210 --> 00:16:04.090
I just mindlessly wiped away my tears

00:15:59.750 --> 00:16:01.420
Calm down...

00:16:01.670 --> 00:16:04.130
The remaining 3 writers should be finished
with their work tomorrow.

00:16:04.580 --> 00:16:09.250
So I'll just finish my part, then it should be possible
to submit the rest for printing one-by-one.

00:16:05.290 --> 00:16:11.210
Words like "I don't believe" or "It doesn't matter what you do"

00:16:10.080 --> 00:16:12.410
Um... um...

00:16:11.880 --> 00:16:15.800
Up until now, we've both hurt each other with them

00:16:12.420 --> 00:16:16.880
That means, if I finish one profile per hour
I should have them all done by morning.

00:16:17.460 --> 00:16:20.000
What a relief, that's super simple!

00:16:18.130 --> 00:16:24.010
But if this is how it ends, we should've been more fearless

00:16:20.170 --> 00:16:24.000
Um... let's see, right now one profile
is about 8 pages long.

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:29.380
For one page... 60 divided by 8 is...
7.5 so that means...

00:16:24.500 --> 00:16:33.080
We should have spent all that time laughing together, the two of us

00:16:29.630 --> 00:16:31.130
1 page done every 7 minutes!

00:16:31.540 --> 00:16:34.040
Right... 1 page in 7 minutes...

00:16:34.210 --> 00:16:39.210
When this swaying train starts moving,

00:16:34.710 --> 00:16:37.750
FINISHING AN ENTIRE PAGE IN SEVEN MINUTES
IS FUCKING IMPOSSIBLE!

00:16:39.210 --> 00:16:41.750
I hear from beyond the window

00:16:40.920 --> 00:16:43.590
I feel sorry for her... she's losing her mind.

00:16:41.920 --> 00:16:45.460
Oh yeah, that cherished song

00:16:43.920 --> 00:16:46.380
She's still got time, it'll be fine.

00:16:47.000 --> 00:16:49.460
When morning comes,

00:16:49.460 --> 00:16:54.710
I hear from far away in the sky between the clouds

00:16:49.750 --> 00:16:52.920
My head hurts... The medicine is wearing off.

00:16:53.460 --> 00:16:56.500
I can't even... I just want to go home and sleep!

00:16:54.710 --> 00:16:58.500
Oh yeah, a sweet voice

00:16:56.500 --> 00:16:59.250
Should I just make a break for it? Like Ito-kun did?

00:16:58.790 --> 00:17:03.870
That's our song, baby

00:17:00.460 --> 00:17:03.040
Oh, that's right! I was supposed
to meet Shinji at that restaurant!

00:17:04.420 --> 00:17:13.550
Shinji
Sorry about last time.
We're meeting at 6:30 tonight, right?
I'm looking forward to
that French place.
-Shinji

00:17:05.380 --> 00:17:08.760
Sorry about last time.
We're meeting at 6:30 tonight, right?
Memories ride the night train

00:17:08.750 --> 00:17:10.540
I'm looking forward to that French place. Shinji
Memories ride the night train

00:17:10.540 --> 00:17:11.620
I'm looking forward to that French place. Shinji

00:17:11.630 --> 00:17:13.550
I'm looking forward to that French place. Shinji
Oh yeah, come on

00:17:13.540 --> 00:17:14.080
Oh yeah, come on

00:17:14.080 --> 00:17:15.040
Sent at 1:30 this afternoon...
Oh yeah, come on

00:17:15.040 --> 00:17:16.370
Sent at 1:30 this afternoon...

00:17:17.000 --> 00:17:19.000
Ah... I completely forgot...

00:17:19.000 --> 00:17:23.580
Shinji

00:17:19.540 --> 00:17:22.170
It's already way past the time
we were supposed to meet...

00:17:22.380 --> 00:17:23.590
and he didn't call.

00:17:24.290 --> 00:17:26.370
Ah... it's all a mess.

00:17:26.380 --> 00:17:27.710
My whole life is.

00:17:28.290 --> 00:17:30.000
I'm just exhausted...

00:17:30.920 --> 00:17:33.670
You're most likely to get sick
when put under stress like that!

00:17:33.880 --> 00:17:36.260
I'm not reckless enough to get sick!

00:17:36.250 --> 00:17:39.210
After all, this is my first chance to prove myself
with a major editorial project.

00:17:40.710 --> 00:17:42.540
But now I'm at my limit...

00:17:43.210 --> 00:17:45.090
It was too early for me to take on
all this responsibility.

00:17:47.130 --> 00:17:51.630
Mimura-san... I wonder how he dealt
with everything when he was my age.

00:17:55.960 --> 00:17:57.420
Yasuyuki Mimura.

00:17:58.290 --> 00:18:01.460
At age 30, he worked for a
major telecommunications company

00:18:01.460 --> 00:18:03.840
and was responsible for numerous projects.

00:18:05.420 --> 00:18:09.340
Back then I was unable to look far enough ahead
and always scrambled to finish things.

00:18:10.540 --> 00:18:13.580
So, even Mimura-san had experiences like this...

00:18:15.380 --> 00:18:16.920
Kohei Hori.

00:18:17.210 --> 00:18:20.040
He was the president
of the game company, SagaSuturn.

00:18:20.750 --> 00:18:24.630
I started the company when I was 20,
but struggled to maintain employees.

00:18:25.080 --> 00:18:28.000
It was more challenging for me
to manage people than do my own work.

00:18:31.250 --> 00:18:32.920
Shinichiro Uemura.

00:18:33.210 --> 00:18:35.500
Professor at the Kanto University of Engineering.

00:18:36.000 --> 00:18:39.170
For some reason or another,
nobody seemed willing to trust me.

00:18:39.580 --> 00:18:42.040
Nobody was ever there to lend me
a hand back then.

00:18:42.920 --> 00:18:44.130
They're all the same...

00:18:44.290 --> 00:18:45.540
Just like me right now.

00:18:46.080 --> 00:18:49.410
Prepared to move forward and get things done,
but nobody around can keep up.

00:18:50.000 --> 00:18:54.330
Yet despite all the struggles they faced,
they found a way through it.

00:18:55.920 --> 00:18:58.420
I felt like I was trapped
in this darkness all by myself.

00:18:59.580 --> 00:19:00.790
But that's not true.

00:19:01.290 --> 00:19:04.960
There were many people before me
who all went through the same thing.

00:19:05.250 --> 00:19:06.830
And overcame it in the end.

00:19:08.080 --> 00:19:08.870
That's it!

00:19:09.330 --> 00:19:12.000
I should use this supplemental issue,
"The Fifty Samurai,"

00:19:12.000 --> 00:19:14.000
to share the reality of that common struggle.

00:19:14.790 --> 00:19:17.210
Nobody starts off being accomplished at their job.

00:19:17.790 --> 00:19:19.750
Everybody struggles with failure.

00:19:19.750 --> 00:19:22.540
But people eventually overcome
the challenges that block their way.

00:19:23.460 --> 00:19:24.790
That's what I need to show.

00:19:25.210 --> 00:19:29.500
And then... I have to overcome
those challenges myself.

00:19:34.460 --> 00:19:37.790
Matsukata, I've got some free time
so I'll help you out.

00:19:37.790 --> 00:19:39.420
I'm okay, but thanks anyway.

00:19:39.920 --> 00:19:41.670
Senpai! Keep up the good work!

00:19:42.040 --> 00:19:43.670
Here are some provisions.

00:19:44.000 --> 00:19:44.580
Thank you.

00:19:45.130 --> 00:19:47.550
Well, it's just some leftovers
from a stakeout I went on.

00:19:47.540 --> 00:19:50.540
Oh, those look tasty. Give some to me, too!

00:19:50.540 --> 00:19:53.250
Huh? Are you sure you want to get even fatter?

00:19:56.830 --> 00:19:57.620
See ya.

00:19:58.420 --> 00:19:59.630
Good work out there today.

00:20:00.080 --> 00:20:02.580
Senpai, are you going to keep working?

00:20:02.580 --> 00:20:03.460
Yeah.

00:20:19.210 --> 00:20:21.210
Matsukata, keep up the good work.

00:20:21.210 --> 00:20:22.380
Thank you.

00:20:22.710 --> 00:20:24.040
Good work today.

00:20:24.040 --> 00:20:25.210
Same to you.

00:20:35.880 --> 00:20:40.130
The remaining 28 profiles
will be ready for print by this afternoon.

00:20:46.000 --> 00:20:46.880
Good work.

00:20:56.880 --> 00:21:02.130
Hiroko Matsukata (29)
Editor for Weekly JIDAI's Special Issue: "The Fifty Samurai"

00:20:57.210 --> 00:21:00.790
Excuse me. You want to take Meiji Street
down to Komaza Street, right?

00:21:00.790 --> 00:21:01.790
Yes.

00:21:03.130 --> 00:21:04.460
Please do.

00:21:04.290 --> 00:21:08.540
Special Issue Now Printing

00:21:05.130 --> 00:21:07.340
Ah... my cold is getting better.

00:21:09.540 --> 00:21:10.580
Good work.

00:21:11.630 --> 00:21:13.510
Thank you very much...

00:21:14.500 --> 00:21:17.830
And so, I whispered my gratitude to Mimura-san.

00:21:31.040 --> 00:21:32.420
Shangri-la

00:21:32.420 --> 00:21:37.670
Yume no naka de sae umaku waraenai kimi no koto

00:21:37.670 --> 00:21:43.000
Dame na hitotte shikari nagara aishiteitai

00:21:46.210 --> 00:21:49.960
Kimi o omouto kyou mo nemurenai

00:21:49.960 --> 00:21:53.540
Bokura doko he mukaouka

00:21:53.540 --> 00:21:59.000
Ahh... ahh...

00:22:00.880 --> 00:22:02.260
Shangri-la

00:22:02.250 --> 00:22:06.210
Shiawasedatte sakende kureyo

00:22:06.210 --> 00:22:10.540
Ijippari na kimi no nakigao misete kureyo

00:22:10.540 --> 00:22:12.210
Shangri-la

00:22:12.210 --> 00:22:17.170
Kimi o omouto kyou mo nemurenai boku no koto

00:22:17.170 --> 00:22:22.210
Dame na hitotte shikarinagara ashitekure

00:22:21.670 --> 00:22:25.460
Shinji
Nice Work Today
Do your best, but don't
wear yourself out.
-Shinji

